# TEST FIXTURE (id 96): the creature-Center nurse and the Mart clerk as model scripts (contract section 17).
# Not part of the game: reached only by the host harness (tools/host_shop, `make -C tools/host_shop`). The content task copies the
# `nurse` / `clerk` scripts into the real centro.map / tienda.map. Flags / vars: var 14 / 15 = the respawn (map id, spawn index) that
# the world reads on a blackout (section 17.4).
@map test_center
@size 8 6
@interior yes
@bg 3
@fill floor_lab
@spawn door 3 4 N          # spawn index 0: the respawn point stored by the nurse (the entrance, like the usual "last Center")
@spawn counter 3 3 N
@legend
  .  tile=floor_lab
  C  tile=none object=wall_corner
  w  tile=none object=wall_j
  y  tile=none object=wall_win_j
  |  tile=none object=wall_i
  q  tile=none object=wall_win_i
  N  npc=lin id=nurse face=S script=nurse
  V  npc=vecino id=clerk face=S script=clerk
@grid
  Cwywwwyw
  |.......
  |..N.V..
  |.......
  |.......
  |.......
# The nurse: ask; YES -> fade to white, the healing-jingle moment, heal the party, remember this Center as the respawn
# point, fade in, say it is done; NO -> good bye.
@script nurse npc
    ask gl.center.ask
    jv 0 1 yes
    say gl.center.bye
    end
  yes:
    fade_out
    wait 1500
    bond heal 0       # contract 65: +1 friendship for every creature that needs the healing (before it is healed)
    heal_party
    respawn door             # = setv respawn_map <this map's id> + setv respawn_spawn <the spawn's index> (vars 14 / 15, section 17.4)
    fade_in
    say gl.center.done
@end
# The clerk: the shop screen (`shop ID` = native 12; ID = a shops.toml name or number, 1 = ciudad_nodo). The shop says good bye itself.
@script clerk npc
    shop ciudad_nodo
@end
